# Spark DS — Accessibility

Spark targets **WCAG 2.1 Level AA**. See `accessibility.html` for full guidance.

## Checklist (every UI change)

- [ ] All interactive elements reachable and operable via keyboard
- [ ] Focus order follows logical reading sequence
- [ ] `:focus-visible` ring using `--semantic-shadow-focus-ring-neutral` or component focus tokens
- [ ] Never use `outline: none` without a visible focus replacement
- [ ] Icon-only controls have `aria-label` (or visible text)
- [ ] Decorative icons use `aria-hidden="true"`
- [ ] Color is not the only indicator of state or errors
- [ ] Form fields have visible `<label>` or `aria-labelledby`
- [ ] Errors include descriptive text, not just red styling
- [ ] Disabled buttons use `disabled` and `aria-disabled="true"`

## React patterns

```tsx
// Icon-only button
<button type="button" aria-label="Delete item" className="spark-btn spark-btn-ghost spark-btn-icon-only spark-btn-medium">
  <TrashIcon aria-hidden="true" />
</button>

// Link styled as button
<a href="/settings" className="spark-btn spark-btn-link spark-btn-medium">Settings</a>
```

## Motion

Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Use `--semantic-motion-*` tokens for transitions defined in Spark.

## Contrast

Normal text: 4.5:1 minimum. Large text and non-text UI: 3:1 minimum. Disabled states are exempt.
